# Near-miss values in why-not, and a disclosure mode

Draft r1 (with the documentation phase added before review), 2026-11-01.
**Awaiting owner review.** Milestone: `why-not-near-misses`.
Source: [gnd-public issue #70](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/70)
(request GR-T8 in the reporter's numbering), plus the owner's direction of
2026-11-01 on disclosure.
Inspection baseline: `33c260e` (main after PR #69).
Planning only. Plan approval, phase execution, implementation and publication
have not occurred.

**Provenance tags.**

- **`(o1)` 2026-11-01:** the owner's direction in session, quoted: "Except for 1
  I think you should go with your recommendations. For 1 I think we need a
  general mode flag. when gnd works in a safe environment meaning it is behind
  the public interface it should not redact. But when it is facing a customer it
  should." The "recommendations" are the five design questions raised on issue
  #70 in the same session; §10 records which rulings this direction covers.
  Item 1 was redaction; its answer is NM-D1 and phase NM2.
- **`(o2)` 2026-11-01:** asked "Four local readers or the six-seat panel?" with
  four local readers offered first, the owner replied, quoted: "yes I also want
  you to add a plan to update the documentation". Read as ruling NM-D9 (four
  local readers) and as the requirement for phase NM4. If "yes" meant something
  else, NM-D9 reverts to open.

A direction on design questions is not approval of the plan.

## Problem and completion predicates

`gnd why-not` names the first step of a clause that left no bindings and up to
five bindings that reached it. When that step is a positive atom, nothing says
what the atom's fact type *does* hold. A join that is empty because one side
spells an entity `ACME CORP.` and the other `Acme Corp.` reads the same as a
join with nothing to meet. The reporter's deletion test localized all 30 gaps
where the missing fact was simply absent, but only 2 of 4 where bound values
existed on both sides and failed to meet; one real failure (an entity name
re-extracted in capitals) was found only by reading a dump.

**What the issue asks for.** A diagnostic, not a change of meaning: for an empty
join, report the join variables and a few values from each side that differ only
by case, whitespace or punctuation. GND keeps exact matching; deciding that two
spellings name one entity stays the caller's job.

**What the owner added `(o1)`.** Near-miss values are population values, so
they fall under redaction. Today GND has two redaction conventions and no
deployment-level switch:

- **Declared redaction** (`src/gnd/redaction.py`): roles a model declares
  sensitive are projected out of check-family outputs (13 `OutputKind`s:
  validate, check, admission, verify, transition, plan, batch, measure, three
  session kinds, population verbalization, diff). Applied by default in the API
  and the CLI; `unredacted=True` or the hidden CLI flag `--unredacted`
  (`commands/_arguments.py:60`, used by 6 parsers, plus `judgments.py:15`)
  retains values. Reports carry `{"mode": "applied" | "unredacted", ...}`.
- **View redaction** (witness lane): `api.witness` and `api.why_not` return raw
  values; the CLI views `witness`, `replay`, `why-not` show no population values
  unless `--raw` (`witness/cli.py:18-40`). `lean` and `souffle` exports also take
  `--raw` (`export/lean_cli.py:18`, `souffle_cli.py:19`).

No environment variable or configuration file selects either today
(`grep environ src/gnd` finds only process plumbing). An operator running GND
behind their own interface has to pass a raw flag on every call; an operator
exposing GND to customers has no way to stop a caller from passing one.

**Outcome.**

1. Each atom blocker in a why-not payload carries a bounded, deterministic list
   of near-miss rows: rows of the blocker's fact type that would have joined if
   string values were compared after a fixed normalization, but do not join
   exactly. Matching stays exact; verdicts, statuses and exits are unchanged.
2. One disclosure mode, set by the operator, decides whether GND emits
   population values across both conventions: `internal` emits them, `customer`
   withholds them and refuses requests for them.

The milestone can close when:

1. On every corpus case, near-misses equal an independent oracle's, the
   exactness invariant holds (no near-miss row matches exactly), and every
   existing why-not golden is unchanged except for the added fields and
   `work.probes`, whose new literal values the NM1 record lists (NM1).
2. Near-miss search is charged against the walk budget with literal-valued
   counter tests on both sides of the ceiling (NM1).
3. In `customer` mode, a leak test over every emitter in both conventions finds
   no population value, and every raw request is refused with exit 3 or a
   `ValueError`; in `internal` mode the same calls return raw values; with the
   mode unset, every existing contract fixture is byte-identical (NM2).
4. `gnd why-not` and `gnd.api.why_not` expose near-misses; the schema ties every
   value-bearing why-not field to `"redacted"` when `view` is `redacted`; pins,
   docs and a release note are updated (NM3).
5. The how-to repair page gains a spelling-gap step built only from payload
   fields, with a negative control (NM3).
6. Every page and packaged skill reference that describes redaction, raw
   values or why-not output has a recorded disposition (edited, cites the one
   home, or unchanged with a reason); the new pages render; every `gnd-run`
   block on a changed page executes; the docs build, link and banned-word checks
   exit 0; the owner has seen the two documentation checkpoints (NM4).
7. Focused gates, independent diff reviews, the question sweep and a PR are
   recorded. Owner acceptance is separate.

## 0. Binding design rules

| Rule | Requirement |
|---|---|
| NM-R1: Exact matching stays the meaning | Near-misses never change a status, blocker, count, exit, extension or any `check`/`witness` payload. Normalization is used only to *find* candidates; the join, identity, negation and comparisons keep the production helpers. A near-miss row that matches exactly is an internal defect, raised as such. |
| NM-R2: One fixed normalization, one home | The normalization is a single function with one normative definition (the NM1 spec, then `docs/reference/why-not.md`). No fuzzy, edit-distance or locale-dependent matching. Non-string values never near-match. |
| NM-R3: Bounded, counted, deterministic | Near-miss search is linear in the blocker's input bindings plus its fact type's rows, charged to the existing walk counters; output order is canonical and the list is capped. Tests assert counters, not wall time. |
| NM-R4: Disclosure is decided once, after the verdict | Mode resolution happens at the public boundary (CLI entry, `gnd.api` function), never in the checker, evaluator or why-not kernel, preserving `redaction.py`'s post-verdict projection boundary. One resolver serves both conventions (standing rule 4: one walk over all emitters, not per-command copies). |
| NM-R5: Unset means today | With no mode set, every output of every command and API function is byte-identical to `33c260e`. Changing a default is a separately recorded compatibility decision, not a side effect. |
| NM-R6: Customer mode is a lock | In `customer` mode an explicit raw request (`--raw`, `--unredacted`, `unredacted=True`, a raw certificate export) is refused, not silently downgraded, so a caller cannot believe it received values it did not. |
| NM-R7: Layering and query policy | New code joins existing homes in `tools/gnd_layers.json` with zero new allowances; model reads follow WN-R7 of the derivation-why-not plan; RF6 allow-list gains no row. |
| NM-R8: Approval, evidence, anonymity | `auto=false`. Plan authorship is not approval. Downstream applications are not named in committed artifacts; `tests/test_why_not_anonymity.py` extends its scan to files added since `33c260e`. |

Each phase spec binds every rule above and every rule in
`.codex/skills/process-phase/references/standing-rules.md`, by name or with a
one-sentence argument that it does not apply.

