## 5. Documentation, skill and compatibility surfaces

- New: two why-not payload fields; one environment variable; one global CLI
  option; one reference page.
- Changed, opt-in only: outputs under `internal` or `customer`. Unset is
  byte-identical (NM-R5).
- No change to `check`, `witness` or `replay` contracts, exit bands, or report
  schemas.
- Release notes, both new pages and every cross-page edit: NM4.

## 6. Risks and required controls

| Risk | Control |
|---|---|
| Near-misses read as "these are the same entity" | Docs and field names say candidate, not match; NM-R1; how-to negative control |
| Normalization drifts between kernel and docs | NM-R2 one home; oracle with its own implementation |
| Quadratic search | NM-R3 index on normalized keys; counter tests |
| A new emitter escapes the mode | NM2-C2 enumerating table test |
| `customer` silently downgrades a raw request | NM-R6 refusal, cased per site |
| Mode leaks into verdicts | NM-R4 resolution only at the boundary; unset parity |
| Unset behaviour changes | NM-R5; NM2-C4 parity |
| Downstream names leak | NM-R8 |
| A repair round introduces defects | §8 stop rule |
| Docs describe the plan rather than the code | Pages written in NM4 after the code; DC1 drafts marked illustrative and not committed; NM4-C5 review against shipped behaviour |
| Docs drift into two homes | NM4-C4 |

## 7. Out of scope

- Fuzzy, edit-distance, phonetic or locale-aware matching; any automatic
  reconciliation of spellings.
- Near-misses for negated atoms, comparisons and head terms (NM-D6).
- Changing any default with the mode unset.
- Re-projecting retained evidence written before a mode was set.
- WN2-R1's other bullets (reason/exit pairing, `refused` nulls, `blocked`
  minItems) and WN2-R2/R3, unless the owner adds them.
- A configuration file; per-tenant modes.
- Publication, release, certification.

## 8. Execution, approval and review protocol

`auto=false`. Each phase follows `process-phase`: spec, owner gate,
implementation and focused tests, an independent diff review, a refactoring
review and a record. No code before recorded spec approval. Plan and close
review instrument: NM-D9. Work happens on a topic branch, then a PR; merge
requires the owner.

## 9. Per-phase verification story

| Phase | Expected result | Focused gate |
|---|---|---|
| NM1 | Oracle agreement; counters; unchanged other fields; no public diff beyond the kernel dict | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_why_not_kernel.py tests/test_why_not_oracle.py tests/test_why_not_anonymity.py tests/test_rf1_layering.py tests/test_rf6_query_policy.py tests/test_gnd_arch.py` |
| NM2 | Leak and refusal per site; unset parity | NM1 gate plus a new `tests/test_disclosure_mode.py`, `tests/test_public_api.py`, `tests/test_rf1_cli_pins.py`, `tests/test_rf5_commands.py`, `tests/test_rf5_handler_pins.py` and the redaction contract tests the NM2 spec names (unresolved until that spec) |
| NM3 | Goldens; schema negatives; docs gates still green | NM2 gate plus `tests/test_public_why_not.py tests/test_why_not_repair_loop.py tests/test_documentation_tutorials.py tests/test_plan_app_docs.py`, `tools/run_tutorials.py`, `zensical build --strict`, `tools/check_docs.py site` |
| NM4 | All pages dispositioned; docs gates; checkpoints seen | NM4-C3 commands plus the one-home grep test |

The broad suite runs on explicit owner selection.

## 10. Owner decisions and open questions

| ID | Question | Readings and cost | Ruling or proposal |
|---|---|---|---|
| NM-D1 | Redaction of near-miss values | (a) follow why-not's view (API raw, CLI redacted); (b) a general disclosure mode across GND | **Ruled `(o1)` 2026-11-01: a general mode.** Its shape (three states, unset = today) is proposed in §2.2 and confirmed at the gate |
| NM-D2 | How the mode is set | (a) env var + global CLI option, no API keyword; (b) also an API keyword: a caller can override a customer deployment; (c) a config file: new discovery surface | proposed **(a)** |
| NM-D3 | Rows with several bound roles | (a) row-level: other bound roles must match exactly or normalized-equal; (b) per role: noisier | **(a)**, recommended in session and covered by `(o1)` |
| NM-D4 | Normalization | §2.1 fixed four steps; no fuzzy matching | **as stated**, `(o1)` |
| NM-D5 | Work and cap | charged to walk counters; 5 pairs; full count | **as stated**, `(o1)` |
| NM-D6 | Which blockers | (a) positive atoms only; (b) also negated atoms | **(a)**, proposed by the plan author; the session raised it without a recommendation, so `(o1)` does not cover it. Confirm at the gate |
| NM-D7 | Resolver home | (a) new `gnd.disclosure` beside `gnd.redaction`; (b) inside `gnd.redaction`, which the checker must never import, so only emitters may | proposed **(a)** |
| NM-D8 | Why-not schema version | (a) `gnd-why-not/2`: the schema is closed (`additionalProperties: false`), so v1 validators reject the new fields; (b) stay `/1`: hosts validating against the shipped v1 schema break silently | proposed **(a)**, with a release-note migration line |
| NM-D9 | Plan and close review instrument | (a) four local readers, as WN-D8; (b) the maintained six-seat panel | **Ruled `(o2)` 2026-11-01: (a)**, with the reading stated in the provenance |
| NM-D11 | Docs checkpoint DC1 before code | (a) drafts after plan approval, before NM2/NM3 code: the owner sees the contract as a reader would and can amend specs cheaply; (b) docs only after code: no illustrative drafts, but late feedback | proposed **(a)** |
| NM-D10 | Customer-mode refusal band | (a) exit 3 (input invalid): the request is invalid for this deployment; (b) a new band: an exit-band change | proposed **(a)** |

No open question is inherited except WN2-R1 (partly owned by NM3-C2).
